  "notes": "Sizes snap to multiples of 32; lengths to 24 fps frames on the 17k+5 grid (5 s = 124 frames). Trained range is about 5-15 s. With `previous`, the new clip repeats the old one's last second: trim 22 frames when cutting them together.",
  "continuation": {
    "param": "previous",
    "overlap_s": 0.9167
  },
  "verified": {
    "date": "2026-10-17",
    "gpu": "RTX 5060 Ti 16 GB, 32 GB RAM (16gb tier: pruned FL2VA int8, NVFP4 text encoder, fp16 VAE, EMA turbo v4; cu130 image, Kitchen attention)",
    "seconds": 69,
    "notes": "Half mode, the MiniMax × LTXV Civitai sample's own shot (its prompt, seed and first frame): 448x576, 7 s (175 frames) in 69 s; the 16:9 Nora shot 672x384 in 46 s; a 576x1024 portrait in 107 s. Peak 15.3 GB VRAM, 15.2 GB RAM. Mastered with ltx25-refine and rtx-master it came out close to the sample. The NVFP4 build this tier used before washed out contrast and changed faces at the same seed, at the same speed (docs/H3-16GB.md §6). Earlier, draft mode with NVFP4: 1344x768, 6 s in 390 s; on an RTX PRO 4500 32 GB (32gb tier) about 7.6 min per 5 s draft."
  }
